   "topic": "Technology",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A low-voltage trench MOSFET with densely packed cells to keep RDS(ON) low, offered for fast switching. Listed applications are battery-powered equipment, solid-state relays and direct interfacing to TTL and CMOS logic levels."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The threshold sits between -1 V and -3 V (-1.6 V typical) at -250 µA. On-resistance is 0.075 Ω typical, 0.19 Ω max at -10 V and -1.9 A, and 0.115 Ω typical, 0.33 Ω max at -4.5 V and -1.4 A. The gate is rated ±20 V, leaks no more than ±100 nA there, and has an internal resistance of 8.5 Ω typical (1.7 to 17 Ω). In Fig.5 RDS(ON) rises steeply below about 3.5 V of gate drive magnitude and falls to near 54 mΩ at 10 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Fig.6 shows on-resistance rising with junction temperature, from about 0.72 of its 25 °C value at -56 °C to about 1.54 at 151 °C. In Fig.2 the 150 °C transfer curve starts conducting at a lower gate voltage than the 25 °C curve and carries less current above the crossing near 3.35 V and 6.8 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Junction-to-ambient thermal resistance is 357 °C/W at steady state, and dissipation is rated 0.35 W at 25 °C ambient. Junction and storage temperatures both span -55 °C to +150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The source-drain diode is rated -0.83 A continuous at 25 °C ambient and -1.75 A at a case temperature of 25 °C, with -10 A pulsed. Forward drop is -0.8 V typical, -1.2 V max at -1.5 A. Recovering from -3 A at 100 A/µs takes 24.5 ns and 4 nC typical."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Switched with a -4.5 V gate generator through 1 Ω into a 10 Ω load at -1.5 A, typical times are 36 ns turn-on delay, 37 ns rise, 12 ns turn-off delay and 9 ns fall. Gate charge to -4.5 V is 2 nC typical, of which 0.6 nC is gate-source and 1 nC gate-drain; to -10 V it is 4 nC. The Miller plateau in Fig.4 sits near 3.9 V, between about 2 nC and 3 nC."
  },
